-- title:
--   Chart functions on the unramified layer: injectivity and descent criterion
-- statement:
--   The setting is the Čerednik–Drinfeld situation over a complete discrete valuation ring.
--
--   Arithmetic data. A prime $r$; a ring $\mathcal{O}$ which is a characteristic-zero domain and a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), with an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`) such that $\mathcal{O}$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), the residue ring $\mathcal{O}/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal{O}$ (`hunr`); a characteristic-zero field $K₀$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   Unramified extension. A characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, together with an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $Fr$ of $Onr$, subject to: $Onr$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`); that ideal is maximal (`hOnr_max`); every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ modulo that ideal (`hOnr_alg`); every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo that ideal (`hOnr_closed`); and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r}$ modulo that ideal for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   Valuation of determinants. A homomorphism $vdet \colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K₀) \to \mathbb{Z}$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $vdet(g) = n$ precisely when $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal{O}$.
--
--   Group data. A group $G$ with a homomorphism $\sigma \colon G \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K₀)$ and a subgroup $\Gamma$ such that some $z \in \Gamma$ has $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix with $vdet(\sigma z) = 2$ (`hcent`) and some $w \in \Gamma$ has $vdet(\sigma w) = 1$ (`hodd`); a subgroup $\Gamma'$ consisting exactly of the elements of $\Gamma$ with $vdet \circ \sigma$ even (`hΓ'`). The homomorphism $\rho \colon G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K₀)$ is the projectivisation of $\sigma$ (`hρ`), and the image $\rho(\Gamma')$ acts on the vertices of the lattice tree of $\mathcal{O}$ in $K₀$ with finite stabilisers (`hdisc`) and with finitely many orbits (`hcocpt`).
--
--   Further data. The matrix $g₁$ is $\mathrm{diag}(\pi, 1)$ (`hg₁`). A subgroup $N \le \rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNle`) whose restriction to $\rho(\Gamma)$ is normal (`hNnorm`) and of nonzero relative index in $\rho(\Gamma')$ (`hNidx`); a Mumford tower `DM : MumfordTower 𝒪 π K₀ r g₁ N`, i.e. a tower $Z_n$ of schemes over $\mathcal{O}/(\pi^{n+1})$, proper and flat over the base, with compatible transition maps forming pullback squares, affine neighbourhoods of finite sets, and a map $q$ sending Deligne data over $\pi^{n+1}$-torsion $\mathcal{O}$-algebras to $Z_n$-points, natural, compatible with the tower, and invariant for the $N$-action, plus open-immersion charts.
--
--   The tower $X$ with its extra structure. Schemes $X_n$ with structure maps $xb_n$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal{O}/(\pi^{n+1}))$ and transitions $xt_n \colon X_n \to X_{n+1}$; a finite group $G₂$ acting by automorphisms $a_n$ on each $X_n$; projections $pr₁{}_n \colon X_n \to Z_n$ and $pr₂{}_n$ to the spectrum of $A_n := E/(\pi^{n+1})$, where $E$ is the equaliser of $Fr^2$ and the identity on $Onr$ (the quadratic descent subring); a homomorphism $\theta \colon \Gamma \to G₂$ and, for each $n$, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra automorphism $Fr₂{}_n$ of $A_n$. The hypotheses on this data are: the squares for $xt_n$ over the base are pullbacks (`hcart`), $xb_n$ is proper (`hproper`) and flat (`hflat`), finite subsets of $X_n$ lie in affine opens (`haff`), the $G₂$-action is over the base (`ha_over`) and commutes with the transitions (`ha_xt`), each $X_n$ is the fibre product of $Z_n$ with $\operatorname{Spec} A_n$ over the base (`hX`), $xb_n$ factors as $pr₁{}_n$ followed by $zb_n$ (`hxb`), the projections are compatible with the transitions (`hxt₁`, `hxt₂`), $\theta$ is surjective (`hθsurj`) with kernel the elements of $\Gamma$ whose image under $\rho$ lies in $N$ (`hθker`), $Fr₂{}_n$ is induced by $Fr$ on the descent subring (`hFr₂`), the action of $\theta(\gamma)$ twists the second projection by $Fr₂{}_n^{-vdet(\sigma\gamma)}$ (`ha_pr₂`), and the action of $\theta(\gamma)$ transports $pr₁$-fibres according to the pullback relation of Deligne data along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$ (`ha_pr₁`).
--
--   The quotient datum. `DQ : TowerQuotientDatum 𝒪 π X xb xt G₂ a` is a tower $Y_n$ over $\mathcal{O}/(\pi^{n+1})$, proper and flat, with cartesian transitions, together with $p_n \colon X_n \to Y_n$ over the base, compatible with the transitions, cartesian against $yt_n$, invariant under the $G₂$-action, finite, surjective, locally epimorphic, and satisfying the local universal property of the quotient. A map $q$ assigning to each $\pi^{n+1}$-torsion $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $B$ and each pair consisting of an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $Onr \to B$ and a Deligne datum over $B$ a $B$-point of $Y_n$, with: `hqdef` identifying $q$ with the composite $x$ followed by $p_n$ whenever $x$ has the prescribed components on $pr₁$ and $pr₂$; `hqover` (the points lie over $\operatorname{Spec} B$), `hqnat` (naturality in $B$), `hqyt` (compatibility with the tower) and `hqinv` ($q$ is constant on pairs related by the twisted $\Gamma$-action $OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct$, i.e. the $Onr$-component is twisted by $Fr^{-vdet(\sigma\gamma)}$ and the Deligne data are related by pullback along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$).
--
--   The unramified layer and its charts. `Pr : MumfordTower.NrPresentation …` provides a tower $X'_n$ over $Onr/(\pi^{n+1})$ with transitions, a $G₂$-action $a'$, a map $qX_n \colon X'_n \to X_n$ exhibiting $X'_n$ as the base change of $X_n$ along $\mathcal{O} \to Onr$, and chart maps $\kappa'_{h,n}$ from the spectrum of $A'_n := \mathrm{chartERing}(Onr, \pi, r)/(\pi^{n+1})$ to $X'_n$, indexed by $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K₀)$; here $\mathrm{chartERing}$ is the localisation of $\mathrm{MvPolynomial}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2, Onr)$ modulo the edge relation away from the discriminant element. Further: $D'$ is a tower quotient datum for $(X', xb', xt', G₂, a')$, with $Y'_n := D'.Y_n$ and $p'_n := D'.p_n$; maps $rY_n \colon Y'_n \to Y_n$ exhibiting $Y'_n$ as the base change of $Y_n$ along $\mathcal{O} \to Onr$ (`hrY`), compatible with the quotient maps (`hrY_p`) and with the transitions (`hrY_yt`). For each $h$ and $n$, $U_{h,n}$ is an open subscheme of $Y'_n$ whose underlying set is the image of the map $\kappa'_{h,n}$ followed by $p'_n$ (`hU`), and $c_{h,n}$ is a ring homomorphism from $\Gamma(U_{h,n}, \mathcal{O}_{Y'_n})$ to $A'_n$; the chart map into $Y'_n$ has the whole source as preimage of $U_{h,n}$ (`hκU`), and $c_{h,n}$ is the pullback of sections along that chart map, identified with an element of $A'_n$ through the canonical isomorphism $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A'_n) \cong A'_n$ (`hc`).
--
--   Conclusion. For every $h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K₀)$ two assertions hold.
--
--   First (injectivity): if $s$ and $s'$ are families of sections $s_m, s'_m \in \Gamma(U_{h,m}, \mathcal{O}_{Y'_m})$, each compatible with the tower in the sense that restricting the pullback of $s_{m+1}$ (respectively $s'_{m+1}$) along $D'.yt_m$ to $U_{h,m}$ gives $s_m$ (respectively $s'_m$), and if $c_{h,m}(s_m) = c_{h,m}(s'_m)$ for all $m$, then $s = s'$.
--
--   Second (characterisation of the image): for every family $(fam_m)_m$ with $fam_m \in A'_m$ which is compatible under the transition maps $A'_{m+1} \to A'_m$, the existence of a compatible family of sections $s$ with $c_{h,m}(s_m) = fam_m$ for all $m$ is equivalent to the following invariance condition. For all $m$, all $\mathcal{O}$-algebras $B$ that are also $Onr$-algebras compatibly, with the image of $\pi$ in $B$ nilpotent, all $Onr$-algebra maps $\bar{x}, \bar{x}' \colon A'_m \to B$, and all Deligne data $d, d', P, P'$ over $B$: if $d$ lies in the edge chart normalised by $\bar{x}$, namely $d$'s line at the standard lattice is spanned by $\bar{x}(\xi) \otimes e_0 + 1 \otimes e_1$, its line at $g₁$ applied to the standard lattice is the image under the base-changed action of $g₁$ of the span of $1 \otimes e_0 + \bar{x}(\eta) \otimes e_1$, and $d$ satisfies $\mathrm{InEdgeChart}$ for the pair $(g₁ \cdot \text{std}, \text{std})$ (edge-nondegeneracy at every prime of $B$); if the same three conditions hold for $d'$ with $\bar{x}'$ in place of $\bar{x}$; if $P$ is the pullback of $d$ along $h^{-1}$ and $P'$ the pullback of $d'$ along $h^{-1}$, in the sense that the lines of the pullback are the comaps of the lines of the original under the base-changed action; and if there exists $\gamma \in \Gamma'$ such that $P'$ is the pullback of $P$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$ in the same sense; then $\bar{x}(fam_m) = \bar{x}'(fam_m)$.
--
--   Here $\xi$ and $\eta$ denote the two chart coordinates `chartERing.ξ` and `chartERing.η` of $\mathrm{chartERing}(Onr, \pi, r)$, reduced modulo $\pi^{m+1}$, and $e_0, e_1$ the standard basis vectors of the standard full lattice.
--
--   This identifies the ring of functions on a chart neighbourhood in the unramified layer of the quotient tower: compatible families of sections over the images of the charts are determined by, and characterised among, compatible families of elements of the chart ring by a $\Gamma'$-invariance condition on the corresponding Deligne data. It is assembled from the injectivity statement and the two implications of the equivalence, and is used in the construction of the descended quotient map on the unramified layer in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation.
